.TH DANBY-VACCINATION 1
.SH NAME
danby-vaccination \- SIR epidemic with an initially vaccinated compartment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/vaccination
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Temple/vaccination
is an interactive live simulation of SIR epidemic with an initially vaccinated compartment.
It integrates the model continuously and redraws its state as parameters or
initial conditions change.
.SH MODEL
S'=-beta SI; I'=beta SI-gamma I; R'=gamma I; V'=0.
.PP
V is the protected initial fraction. Coverage reallocates the noninfected initial population between S and V.
.SH DISPLAY
Four time traces show S, I, R, and V. Increasing coverage suppresses the infection peak; the simple model assumes perfect permanent protection.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag vertically to seed infection. Bottom tracks set contact, recovery, and coverage.
.PP
Space pauses or resumes the simulation.  Period advances one displayed step
while paused.  The
.B r
key restores the default initial state and
.B q
or Escape exits.
.SH INTERPRETATION
The quantities are normalized unless physical units are stated explicitly.
The display is a visualization of a low-dimensional differential-equation
model, not an agent simulation or a prediction of a particular real system.
Parameter changes restart the displayed history so trajectories from different
settings are not joined.
.SH NUMERICS
The state is advanced by the general-purpose
.B Numerics
fourth-order Runge-Kutta solver.  Small negative values caused by numerical
roundoff are clamped for nonnegative population and stock models.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/vaccination.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR numerics (2)

